## 🔍 Checks

| Check | Category | What it detects |
|---|---|---|
| **Speed** | Movement | Moving faster than sprint speed + potion allowance |
| **Fly** | Movement | Staying airborne beyond server-confirmed air ticks |
| **KillAura** | Combat | High CPS, multi-target attacks, attacking while looking away |
| **AutoClicker** | Combat | CPS > 16 and robotic click interval pattern (low variance) |
| **AutoTotem** | Combat | Re-equipping a totem faster than humanly possible (<100ms) |
| **CrystalAura** | Combat | Placing or exploding end crystals at inhuman speed |
| **NoFall** | Movement | Client claims to be on ground while server says airborne |
| **Reach** | Combat | Attacking entities beyond 3.2 blocks (with ping compensation) |
| **Scaffold** | World | Placing blocks at inhuman speed or impossible angles |
| **Timer** | Movement | Sending more than 22 movement packets per second |
| **Jesus** | Movement | Walking on water surface |
| **NoKnockback** | Combat | Not responding to server-sent velocity (knockback resistance) |

> All checks use **raw packet data** — not Bukkit events. This means the client cannot fake `onGround`, position, or timing values.

